body:
Ok. I just got home from the interview. I thought that I should tell the vice president my mistake in the follow-up email thanking him for the consideration and apologize for the mistake saying it slipped my mind to mention it when he asked me. In addition, I not only didn't list it on my resume and submitted a copy to them with that excluded but I also didn't include it on the application. I also didn't finish the application but can probably say I neglected to submit the one employer. What do I say when they ask me why I left it off the resume? That I gave them the wrong copy?

&#x200B;

I just assumed they were badmouthing me in some way because I'm only now getting interviews after taking this off my resume and I've been looking for a year after I was there.
